  <!-- ============ SECTION 14 – GLOSSARY ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">General price index</div><div class="glossary-def">An index reflecting changes in the general purchasing power of a currency, used to restate financial statement amounts.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Monetary items</div><div class="glossary-def">Money held and assets/liabilities to be received or paid in fixed or determinable amounts of money.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Non-monetary items</div><div class="glossary-def">Items that are not monetary items – generally restated for inflation using a general price index.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Net monetary position</div><div class="glossary-def">The difference between an entity's monetary assets and monetary liabilities, exposed to purchasing-power gains/losses.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Carrying amount</div><div class="glossary-def">The SOFP-recognized amount of an asset (net of accumulated depreciation/impairment) or a liability.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Measuring unit current at the reporting date</div><div class="glossary-def">The purchasing-power basis to which all restated financial statement amounts are expressed.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">SOFP</span> Statement of financial position
      <span class="badge bp">SOFPerf</span> Statement of financial performance
      <span class="badge be">NA/E</span> Net assets/equity (statement of changes)
    </div>
  </div>

  
